<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Q3 current account deficit $713 mln.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Q3 current account deficit $713 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico posted a current account deficit of $713 million in the third quarter, compared with a deficit of $267 million in the same period in 1995, Banco de Mexico said on Monday.</p>
<p>In the first nine months, the deficit was $234 million, compared with a deficit of $1.018 billion in the January-September period the year before, it added.  </p>
<p>It said the Q3 deficit comprised surpluses in the trade balance and transfers, and of deficits in non-factor and factor services.</p>
<p>The following table details the current account balance of payments. All figures are in billions of dollars:</p>
<p>				  1995		  1996</p>
<p>			     Q3	Q1-Q3	Q3     Q1-Q3</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    Overall Balance  -0.267   -1.018     -0.713  -0.234</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>    Trade Balance    +2.214   +5.410     +1.422  +5.564</p>
<p>	Exports	 +20.087  +58.505    +24.258 +69.741</p>
<p>	Imports	 -17.873  -53.095    -22.836 -64.177</p>
<p>    Non-factor Svcs  +0.017   +0.852     -0.041  +0.847</p>
<p>    Factor Services  -3.572  -10.311     -3.291 -10.058</p>
<p>    Transfers	  +1.074   +3.031     +1.197  +3.413</p>
<p>-- Henry Tricks, Mexico City newsroom +525 728-9560</p>
